<article class="env-lemma" id="036N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/036N">Lemma <span data-tag="036N">35.28.1</span>.</a> The property $\mathcal{P}(f)=$“$f$ is locally of finite presentation” is fppf local on the source. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Being locally of finite presentation is Zariski local on the source and the target, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01TQ" data-tag="01TQ">29.22.2</a>. It is a property which is preserved under composition, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01TR" data-tag="01TR">29.22.3</a>. This proves (1), (2) and (3) of Lemma <a href="/tag/036H" data-tag="036H">35.26.4</a>. The final condition (4) is Lemma <a href="/tag/02KK" data-tag="02KK">35.14.1</a>. Hence we win. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>